# 🚀 KUBEADM SETUP

## 🔹 MASTER NODE FLOW

1. Disable swap
2. Install containerd + docker
3. Install kubeadm, kubelet, kubectl
4. Initialize cluster:

kubeadm init --pod-network-cidr=192.168.0.0/16

5. Configure kubectl:

mkdir -p ~/.kube
cp /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf ~/.kube/config
chown $(id -u):$(id -g) ~/.kube/config

6. Generate join command:

kubeadm token create --print-join-command > join.sh

---

## 🔹 WORKER NODE FLOW

1. Same setup (docker, kubeadm, etc.)
2. Fetch join.sh from master
3. Execute:

bash join.sh

---

## 🔹 VERIFY CLUSTER

kubectl get nodes

Expected:

* master → Ready
* workers → Ready

